{
  "_comment": "Colloquial <-> clinical condition names, for meds.for_condition(). A layperson asks 'what did she get for a cold' but a discharge summary says 'AURTI' or 'URTI' -- a literal substring search matches neither to the other. Each bucket now carries a standard ICD-10-CM identity (icd10 = 3-char category list + icd10_title); the bucket KEY stays the runtime identity (consumers key on it, exactly as analytes key on name). Aliases are the fuzzy layer: token-containment against BOTH diagnoses and free-text reason. Buckets are 1:1 with an ICD-10-CM category; a colloquial umbrella phrase ('heart disease', 'stomach bug', 'skin rash') is repeated as an alias across the clinical children it spans, so expand() still widens across all of them. Hand-curated, generic medical terminology only: no names, no dates, no real diagnoses (see CLAUDE.md). Codes are ICD-10-CM (US public-domain), verified against data/icd10cm.csv by tools/conditions_coverage.py.",
